18. Glue Job Retry Strategies

GLUE JOB CONFIGURATION:
├── MaxRetries: Number of times to retry on failure (0-10)
│   └── Default: 0 (no retry)
├── Timeout: Max minutes before job is killed
│   └── Default: 2880 minutes (48 hours)
├── Job run notification: EventBridge on state change
└── Error handling: Catch exceptions in script → log → continue or fail

RETRY BEHAVIOR:
├── Retry happens on ANY failure (OOM, network, code error)
├── Each retry is a FULL re-execution (from scratch)
├── Job Bookmarks help avoid reprocessing on retry
│   └── Retry starts from where bookmarks left off
├── MaxRetries = 3 means: 1 original + 3 retries = 4 total attempts
└── Exponential backoff: NOT built-in (retries immediately)

BEST PRACTICES:
├── Set MaxRetries = 1-3 for transient failures (network, throttling)
├── Set Timeout to 2x expected duration (catch runaway jobs)
├── Use Job Bookmarks so retries don't reprocess old data
├── Monitor with EventBridge: trigger alert after final retry fails
└── For complex retry logic → use Step Functions (Retry with BackoffRate)

STEP FUNCTIONS vs GLUE RETRIES:
├── Simple retry → Glue MaxRetries (sufficient)
├── Retry with exponential backoff → Step Functions Retry
├── Retry only specific error types → Step Functions Catch
├── Conditional retry (retry OOM but not code errors) → Step Functions
└── Notification between retries → Step Functions + SNS

EXAM TRIGGER:
├── "Glue job fails intermittently due to network" → MaxRetries = 2-3
├── "Job runs forever" → Set Timeout
├── "Retry with exponential backoff" → Step Functions (not Glue native)
├── "Don't reprocess data on retry" → Job Bookmarks
└── "Alert after all retries exhausted" → EventBridge FAILED state → SNS

