8. S3 Object Lock (WORM)

WHAT: Write Once, Read Many — prevents deletion/modification
WHEN: Regulatory compliance (SEC, FINRA, healthcare)

MODES:
├── Governance Mode:
│   ├── Most users can't delete/overwrite
│   ├── Users with special permissions CAN override
│   └── Use: Internal compliance (flexible)
│
├── Compliance Mode:
│   ├── NOBODY can delete/overwrite (not even root account!)
│   ├── Cannot be shortened or removed until retention expires
│   └── Use: Regulatory requirements (SEC Rule 17a-4)
│
└── Legal Hold:
    ├── Prevents deletion regardless of retention period
    ├── Can be placed/removed by authorized users
    └── Use: Litigation hold (preserve evidence)

RETENTION PERIOD:
├── Set per-object or as bucket default
├── Specifies how long the object is protected
└── After expiry: normal S3 behavior resumes

REQUIREMENTS:
├── Bucket must have versioning ENABLED
├── Object Lock must be enabled at bucket creation (cannot add later)
└── Works with all storage classes

EXAM TRIGGER:
├── "Regulatory compliance, data cannot be deleted" → Object Lock (Compliance mode)
├── "SEC 17a-4 / FINRA" → Object Lock Compliance mode
├── "Prevent accidental deletion but allow admin override" → Governance mode
