5. Glue Schema Registry

WHAT: Central schema management for streaming data (Avro, JSON Schema, Protobuf)
WHERE: Works with Kinesis, MSK, Glue Streaming, Lambda

WHY IT MATTERS:
├── Producers and consumers agree on data format
├── Schema evolution: add/remove fields safely
├── Compatibility modes prevent breaking changes
├── Reduces serialization/deserialization errors

COMPATIBILITY MODES:
├── BACKWARD: New schema can READ old data (add optional fields, remove fields)
├── FORWARD: Old schema can READ new data (remove optional fields, add fields)
├── FULL: Both backward AND forward compatible
├── NONE: No compatibility checks (dangerous)
└── BACKWARD is most common (new consumers read old + new data)

HOW IT WORKS:
├── Producer registers schema → gets schema version ID
├── Producer embeds version ID in each record (header)
├── Consumer reads version ID → fetches schema from registry
├── Consumer deserializes using correct schema version
└── If schema change violates compatibility → registration REJECTED

EXAM TRIGGER:
├── "Ensure schema compatibility in Kafka/Kinesis pipeline" → Glue Schema Registry
├── "Prevent breaking changes in streaming data" → Schema Registry + BACKWARD compatibility
├── "Schema evolution for Avro data" → Schema Registry
├── "Producers and consumers use different schema versions" → Schema Registry handles it
└── "Validate schema before publishing" → Schema Registry compatibility check

